  "inputs": {
    "manifest": {
      "specVersion": "1",
      "id": "lax-379983",
      "leanVersion": "v4.33.0",
      "mathlibVersion": "db584cd6d46c92f209a44c0f1c829460d327499d",
      "title": "Feedback vertex and edge numbers",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Jakub Balabán"
        },
        {
          "name": "OpenAI Codex"
        }
      ],
      "bibEntries": []
    },
    "abstract": "For a finite undirected simple graph, the feedback vertex number is the minimum\nnumber of vertices whose deletion makes the graph acyclic, and the feedback\nedge number is the corresponding minimum number of edges. We prove that the\nfeedback vertex number is at most the feedback edge number.\n"
  },
  "requiredByConcepts": [],
  "requiredByProofs": [],
  "concepts": [
    {
      "id": "Lax379983.FeedbackEdgeNumber",
      "path": "concepts/Lax379983/FeedbackEdgeNumber.lean",
      "title": "Feedback edge number",
      "type": "definition",
      "description": "Let $G=(V,E)$ be a finite undirected simple graph. A feedback edge set is a\nset $F\\subseteq E$ for which the graph $G-F$, obtained by deleting the edges\nin $F$ and retaining all vertices, is acyclic. The feedback edge number is\n$$\n\\operatorname{FEN}(G)=\\min\\{\\lvert F\\rvert : F\\subseteq E,\\;\nG-F\\text{ is acyclic}\\}.\n$$\nThe minimum exists because deleting all edges leaves an acyclic graph.",
      "imports": [],
      "mathlibImports": [
        "Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.Acyclic",
        "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Lattice",
        "Mathlib.Data.Set.Card"
      ],
      "sourceText": "import Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.Acyclic\nimport Mathlib.Data.Nat.Lattice\nimport Mathlib.Data.Set.Card\n\n/-!\n---\ntitle: Feedback edge number\ntype: definition\n---\nLet $G=(V,E)$ be a finite undirected simple graph. A feedback edge set is a\nset $F\\subseteq E$ for which the graph $G-F$, obtained by deleting the edges\nin $F$ and retaining all vertices, is acyclic. The feedback edge number is\n$$\n\\operatorname{FEN}(G)=\\min\\{\\lvert F\\rvert : F\\subseteq E,\\;\nG-F\\text{ is acyclic}\\}.\n$$\nThe minimum exists because deleting all edges leaves an acyclic graph.\n-/\n\nnamespace Lax379983.FeedbackEdgeNumber\n\n/-- The minimum number of edges whose deletion makes the graph acyclic. -/\nnoncomputable def feedbackEdgeNumber {V : Type*} [Finite V] (G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ :=\n  sInf {n : ℕ | ∃ F : Set (Sym2 V),\n    F ⊆ G.edgeSet ∧ F.ncard = n ∧ (G.deleteEdges F).IsAcyclic}\n\nend Lax379983.FeedbackEdgeNumber\n",
      "statements": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Lax379983.FeedbackNumberComparison",
      "path": "concepts/Lax379983/FeedbackNumberComparison.lean",
      "title": "Feedback vertex number is at most feedback edge number",
      "type": "theorem",
      "description": "For every finite undirected simple graph $G$,\n$$\n\\operatorname{FVN}(G)\\leq\\operatorname{FEN}(G).\n$$\nNo connectedness or nonemptiness assumption is required.",
      "imports": [
        "Lax379983.FeedbackEdgeNumber",
        "Lax379983.FeedbackVertexNumber"
      ],
      "mathlibImports": [],
      "sourceText": "import Lax379983.FeedbackVertexNumber\nimport Lax379983.FeedbackEdgeNumber\n\n/-!\n---\ntitle: Feedback vertex number is at most feedback edge number\ntype: theorem\n---\nFor every finite undirected simple graph $G$,\n$$\n\\operatorname{FVN}(G)\\leq\\operatorname{FEN}(G).\n$$\nNo connectedness or nonemptiness assumption is required.\n-/\n\nnamespace Lax379983.FeedbackNumberComparison\n\nopen Lax379983.FeedbackVertexNumber Lax379983.FeedbackEdgeNumber\n\n/-- Every finite simple graph has feedback vertex number at most its feedback edge number. -/\naxiom feedbackVertexNumber_le_feedbackEdgeNumber {V : Type*} [Finite V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) : feedbackVertexNumber G ≤ feedbackEdgeNumber G\n\nend Lax379983.FeedbackNumberComparison\n",
      "statements": [
        {
          "id": "Lax379983.FeedbackNumberComparison.feedbackVertexNumber_le_feedbackEdgeNumber",
          "signature": "feedbackVertexNumber_le_feedbackEdgeNumber : ∀ {V : Type u_1} [inst : Finite V] (G : SimpleGraph V),\n  instLENat.le (Lax379983.FeedbackVertexNumber.feedbackVertexNumber G)\n    (Lax379983.FeedbackEdgeNumber.feedbackEdgeNumber G)",
          "startLine": 20,
          "endLine": 22,
          "doc": "Every finite simple graph has feedback vertex number at most its feedback edge number."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Lax379983.FeedbackVertexNumber",
      "path": "concepts/Lax379983/FeedbackVertexNumber.lean",
      "title": "Feedback vertex number",
      "type": "definition",
      "description": "Let $G=(V,E)$ be a finite undirected simple graph. A feedback vertex set is a\nset $S\\subseteq V$ for which the induced graph $G[V\\setminus S]$ is acyclic.\nThe feedback vertex number is\n$$\n\\operatorname{FVN}(G)=\\min\\{\\lvert S\\rvert : S\\subseteq V,\\;\nG[V\\setminus S]\\text{ is acyclic}\\}.\n$$\nThe minimum exists because deleting all vertices leaves an acyclic graph.",
      "imports": [],
      "mathlibImports": [
        "Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.Acyclic",
        "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Lattice",
        "Mathlib.Data.Set.Card"
      ],
      "sourceText": "import Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.Acyclic\nimport Mathlib.Data.Nat.Lattice\nimport Mathlib.Data.Set.Card\n\n/-!\n---\ntitle: Feedback vertex number\ntype: definition\n---\nLet $G=(V,E)$ be a finite undirected simple graph. A feedback vertex set is a\nset $S\\subseteq V$ for which the induced graph $G[V\\setminus S]$ is acyclic.\nThe feedback vertex number is\n$$\n\\operatorname{FVN}(G)=\\min\\{\\lvert S\\rvert : S\\subseteq V,\\;\nG[V\\setminus S]\\text{ is acyclic}\\}.\n$$\nThe minimum exists because deleting all vertices leaves an acyclic graph.\n-/\n\nnamespace Lax379983.FeedbackVertexNumber\n\n/-- The minimum number of vertices whose deletion makes the graph acyclic. -/\nnoncomputable def feedbackVertexNumber {V : Type*} [Finite V] (G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ :=\n  sInf {n : ℕ | ∃ S : Set V, S.ncard = n ∧ (G.induce Sᶜ).IsAcyclic}\n\nend Lax379983.FeedbackVertexNumber\n",
      "statements": []
    }
  ],
  "proofs": [
    {
      "id": "Lax379983Proofs.feedbackVertexNumber_le_feedbackEdgeNumber",
      "path": "proofs/Lax379983Proofs/FeedbackNumberComparison.lean",
      "conclusion": "Lax379983.FeedbackNumberComparison.feedbackVertexNumber_le_feedbackEdgeNumber",
      "assumptions": [],
      "description": "Choose a minimum feedback edge set $F$ and one endpoint of each edge in $F$.\nThe set $S$ of chosen endpoints has cardinality at most $|F|$. Every edge of\nthe induced graph $G[V\\setminus S]$ remains in $G-F$, so this induced graph\nis acyclic. Thus $S$ is a feedback vertex set and\n$\\operatorname{FVN}(G)\\leq |S|\\leq |F|=\\operatorname{FEN}(G)$."
    }
  ],
